-- title:
--   Exactly ℓ stable lifts of a level-N subgroup
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b \in \mathbb{Q}$ and let $q \neq q'$ be primes such that $B = \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`, i.e. $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$ every nonzero element of $B \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit exactly when $v$ contains $q$ or $q'$. Let $\Lambda \subset B$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is a maximal order: it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $B$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, is finitely generated, and any order containing it equals it. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \neq q, q'$, and let $N \geq 1$ with $\ell \mid N$. Let $M$ be an abelian group equipped with a map $\rho$ from $\Lambda$ to the additive endomorphisms of $M$ sending $1$ to the identity, respecting products (whenever the product of two elements of $\Lambda$ is taken in $\Lambda$) in the sense $\rho(xy) = \rho(x) \circ \rho(y)$, and additive in the argument. Assume $M$ is generated by a single element $P_0$, so that every $P \in M$ is $\rho(m)P_0$ for some $m \in \Lambda$, and that $\rho(m)P_0 = 0$ holds exactly when $m = N\ell \cdot m'$ for some $m' \in \Lambda$. Let $C \leq M$ be a subgroup stable under all $\rho(n)$, $n \in \Lambda$, together with a bijection $\mathbb{Z}/N \times \mathbb{Z}/N \simeq C$ that is additive, and let $S_0 \leq M$ be a subgroup stable under all $\rho(n)$ with an additive bijection $\mathbb{Z}/N\ell \times \mathbb{Z}/N\ell \simeq S_0$ and with $\ell \cdot Q \in C$ for all $Q \in S_0$. Then the set of subgroups $S \leq M$ which are stable under all $\rho(n)$, satisfy $C = \ell S$ (every $P \in C$ is $\ell Q$ for some $Q \in S$, and conversely), and whose $\ell$-torsion lies in $C$, is finite of cardinality exactly $\ell$.
--
--   This is the group-theoretic counting step behind the degree of the degeneracy map between moduli of fake elliptic curves with level structure: a $\Lambda$-stable level-$N$ subgroup of a cyclic $\Lambda/N\ell\Lambda$-module admits exactly $\ell$ $\Lambda$-stable level-$N\ell$ lifts when $\ell \mid N$ and $\ell$ is unramified in $B$. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.natCard_levelExt_eq_of_dvd`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.natCard_levelExt_eq_of_dvd), where $M$ is the group of $N\ell$-torsion points of a fake elliptic curve, and it rests on the identification of $\Lambda/\ell\Lambda$ with $M_2(\mathbb{F}_\ell)$.
